<title>BELGIUM: Council adopts &quot;Barber&quot; pension amendments.</title>
<headline>Council adopts &quot;Barber&quot; pension amendments.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Social Affairs Council adopted a directive on Monday to bring EU law into line with a landmark court decision requiring companies to give men and women equal treatment in company pension schemes.</p>
<p>The legislation, COM(95)186, would amend Directive 86/378/EEC on occupational social security schemes to ensure that provisions on retirement age and survivors' benefits apply equally to both sexes.</p>
<p>The existing directive allows member states to exclude those aspects.</p>
<p>The European Court of Justice said in its 1990 &quot;Barber&quot; judgment (Case 262/88) and subsequent rulings that sex discrimination in company pension plans violated Article 119 of the EC treaty requiring that men and women receive equal pay for equal work.</p>
</text>
